// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
//! expander.resource's functions: the board's IO expander - the pins the
//! panel, the touch controller and the SD card are held by, the backlight
//! and an analogue input. A resource: no Open or Close, its first function
//! in the first slot. The base comes from OpenResource("expander.resource").
##include resources/expander as expander
##basetype ExpanderBase
##name expander.resource
##bias 0
##public
/// Take `pin` (0 to PIN_COUNT-1) for `name`, which is kept for the listing
/// and must outlive the claim. False if the pin is out of range or someone
/// else already holds it. A driver claims the pins it is going to drive so
/// that two of them fighting over one is an error at claim time rather than
/// a light that goes out when an unrelated card is initialised.
bool ClaimPin(u32 pin, [*:0]const u8 name)
/// Give `pin` back. Its level is left as it is.
void ReleasePin(u32 pin)
/// Who holds `pin`, or null if nobody does.
?[*:0]const u8 PinOwner(u32 pin)
/// Drive `pin` high or low. The pin becomes an output if it was not one,
/// its value being written before the direction changes so that it never
/// drives the wrong level first. False if the pin is out of range or the
/// part does not answer.
bool SetPin(u32 pin, bool high)
/// What `pin` reads: 0 or 1, or -1 if the pin is out of range or the part
/// does not answer.
i32 GetPin(u32 pin)
/// The backlight, BACKLIGHT_OFF (0) to BACKLIGHT_FULL (100). The register
/// behind it counts the other way, which this hides. False if the part does
/// not answer.
bool SetBacklight(u32 percent)
/// What SetBacklight was last given.
u32 Backlight()
/// The analogue input, 0 to 65535, or -1 if the part does not answer.
i32 ReadADC()
##end
